# Cachy environment configuration — copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored. Never commit real secrets.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Shared secret between the browser and this server's API routes.
#
# Guards 17 routes, including /api/orders, /api/tpsl, /api/positions,
# /api/account, /api/balance, every /api/sync/* endpoint and the three AI
# proxies (/api/ai/anthropic, /api/ai/gemini, /api/ai/openai).
#
# Authentication FAILS CLOSED: if this is unset, all of those routes answer 401
# and the app cannot talk to its own backend. That is deliberate — an unset
# secret is a misconfiguration, not a permission grant. Without it a public
# deployment would be an open relay, with AI calls billed to the operator.
# See docs/adr/0002-api-authentication-fails-closed.md.
#
# The same value goes into the app's Settings → Connections → App Access Token,
# so the browser can send it as the `x-app-access-token` header.
#
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
APP_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Enables the /api/stream-logs endpoint. Leave unset to keep log streaming off;
# the endpoint denies access in production when this is missing.
# LOG_STREAM_KEY=

# Storage path for the legacy file-based chat store. Must resolve inside the
# project directory. Defaults to db/chat_messages.json.
# Note: that store is currently orphaned — Global Chat runs on SpacetimeDB.
# See docs/ROADMAP.md item 12.
# CHAT_DB_PATH=db/chat_messages.json

# Node environment. Set to `production` for deployed instances.
# NODE_ENV=development

# Server-side AI keys, used by /api/sentiment. These stay on the server.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A NOTE ON VITE_-PREFIXED VARIABLES
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_-prefixed variable into the client bundle at build
# time, so anything named that way is public: it is served as plain JavaScript to
# every visitor. Never put a secret behind a VITE_ name.
#
# The AI key settings once defaulted to VITE_OPENAI_API_KEY / VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY
# / VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. That fallback is gone (roadmap item 24a) — setting
# those variables now has no effect. Each user enters their own key in
# Settings → AI; those keys are Class A data under ADR-0001 and stay in the
# browser's localStorage.
#
# Only VITE_APP_VERSION is set today, by vite.config.ts from package.json.
